From bd896631871398f88d9809c5b25dcbd88e9f5213 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:44:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel material properties: version 3 of the
 generated functions

For a material property S, the interface generates
`int S_generic_parallel(mfront_gpmp_OutputStatus*, const mfront_gpmp_BatchData*)`
and `int S_generic_parallel_report(mfront_gpmp_OutputStatus*, const mfront_gpmp_Statistics*)`.

- the data of a batch (`mfront_gpmp_BatchData`) give the number of points,
  the output and the arguments (pointer and stride), the out of bounds
  policy, the optional statuses of the points and the execution options.
  The function with contiguous arrays (suffix 2) is removed;
- the names end with `_generic_parallel`: the names of the material
  properties can't contain `_generic_parallel`, and a library is recognized
  by the `S_generic_parallel_api_version` symbol (version 3);
- the evaluation at each point is the one of the generic interface: same
  status at each point (0, 1, -1 or -4), same retained check (first failure,
  otherwise last warning), NaN for -1, computed value for -4;
- the output status gives the numbers and the first points of the failures
  and of the unreliable results. Its status is the error of the batch,
  otherwise the status of the first failed point, otherwise the status of the
  first unreliable point. The statistics hold opaque keys (index of the point
  and check), decoded by the report function, which takes no policy;
- errors of the batch: -5 (invalid arguments, including more than 2^48 - 1
  points and a uniform output with several points), -6 (invalid parameters),
  -7 (runtime error of the backend, including the exceptions thrown on the
  host). As with the generic interface, the number of arguments is not
  checked if the runtime checks are disabled;
- with statistics, on all the backends, the output status only reports the
  errors of the batch and the report function gives the result;
- the sycl backend copies the statuses of the points as the output;
- no exception goes through the generated functions: their bodies are
  enclosed in a `try` block, and an unexpected exception gives -7;
- the number of blocks of the kernels of the cuda and hip backends is
  checked (-5 beyond 2^31 - 1 blocks) instead of being truncated;
- the statistics given by the execution options must be readable by the
  host, which reads them in the report function (documentation).

The documentation and the release notes are updated.
